1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,160
Is it possible to sell $100 million worth of books

2
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,840
and break the Guinness World Record

3
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:06,120
for the biggest launch ever?

4
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:09,080
Well, on August 16th of 2025, I tried and this would happen.

5
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:10,000
So after doing some research,

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,640
I figured out who the record holders were

7
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:13,520
for the best-selling non-fiction launch of all time.

8
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,160
And they were literally presidents, monarchs,

9
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:15,980
and politicians.

10
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:16,820
And since we're trying to do something

11
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:17,920
that no one else has ever done before,

12
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:20,320
I knew I had to do work that no one had ever done before.

13
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:22,000
So step one was I actually wrote the book.

14
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:22,920
That was the easiest part.

15
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:25,120
This was my third book in the $100 million series.

16
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,320
First, you write your offer,

17
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:27,600
then you advertise your offer,

18
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:28,640
and then you monetize your offer.

19
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:30,320
Step two is you make the offers.

20
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,120
So we created 17 different things

21
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:34,760
in order to actually accompany the book

22
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:36,160
to make it even more valuable.

23
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:37,760
Step three is make value-added bonuses.

24
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:39,920
So I made a 24-chapter secret playbook

25
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:42,480
and 12 playbooks that were 600 pages in total.

26
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,200
Step four is marketing assets.

27
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,480
So I wrote 10 different landing pages, six VSLs,

28
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:48,480
400 pages of email and text copy,

29
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:52,760
1,700 slides for the presentation, and over 3,000 ads.

30
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,160
Step five, damage control.

31
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:56,400
So we took backup plans for all potential choke points.

32
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,440
Number one, if we got suspended from an advertising platform,

33
00:00:58,440 --> 00:00:59,880
our Google Ads account got down.

34
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:02,320
Emails and text not going through with the link to go live,

35
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:04,640
the live link not working, payment processing not working.

36
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,040
Our Shopify link was sending people to Serbia.

37
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:09,040
Step six, we trained the sales team.

38
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:11,320
So we pulled the salespeople and non-salespeople,

39
00:01:11,320 --> 00:01:13,040
and we trained them on the book launch offer

40
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:14,120
so that they could handle the phones.

41
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,800
And we had 700 people who were handling the phones

42
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:17,800
over three days.

43
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,320
Number seven, set up and prep.

44
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:20,920
So we built our set in the headquarters

45
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:22,080
rather than doing it in a vendor.

46
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:23,440
I practiced the presentation.

47
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:24,680
I can't even tell you how many times,

48
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,560
but literally, at what point am I gonna move this book?

49
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:28,760
And I had to be able to talk and move at the same time,

50
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,240
and believe me, the first times, it sucked.

51
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:31,880
Step eight was the actual event itself.

52
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:33,480
Everybody, everybody quiet on set.

53
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:36,280
We're going live in five, four, three.

54
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:39,360
I'm Alex Samosi, and welcome to my $100 million

55
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:41,240
Money Models book launch event.

56
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:42,920
So just a few hours into the event,

57
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,840
we sold 1.4 million copies and broke

58
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:45,760
the Guinness World Record.

59
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:48,520
And so we went live on Friday, Saturday, and Sunday,

60
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:51,600
over those 72 hours and sold 3.6 million copies

61
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,600
that generated $106 million in sales.

62
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:54,560
If you like this kind of stuff,

63
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,280
follow to see whatever crazy thing we do next,

64
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,880
because it will be even crazier.

